{:id "0048-score-eval"
 :title "Score eval: measure whether an agent can write valid, varied scores from one page of reference"
 :lupa/deps #{"0046-lab-score-pace" "0047-site"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "Hypothesis H4 in docs/product/lab-notebook.md: the full score
        language is for agents, so an agent given one page of reference
        (resources/agent/score-reference.md) should write scores that are
        valid on the first try and that change with what it means. Build
        the harness that asks, checks and counts. The foreman runs it and
        records the numbers; tests use canned replies and make no model
        calls."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/dev/score_eval.clj" "test/halfahead/dev/score_eval_test.clj"
         "bb.edn"]
 :design "Inputs, written by the foreman (read them, do not edit):
          resources/agent/score-reference.md (the page an agent is given)
          and resources/eval/score-cases.edn (28 cases: :mark, the text is
          fixed and a :feeling is given; :compose, the agent answers :said
          with its own text; :patch, the text is fixed and :brief asks for
          a written-out patch).
          halfahead.dev.score-eval (.clj). Pure:
          (prompt case reference) -> {:system s :user u}. The system
            prompt is one line ('You are an agent in a conversation where
            text is performed, not only shown.') and then the reference,
            verbatim. The user prompt: for :mark, the text (to be used
            unchanged as \"text\") and 'What you mean by it:' with the
            feeling's name and its two numbers from lab.marks/feelings as
            words (for example 'tender: calm and warm'); for :compose,
            'Someone said:' and the :said text, and 'Reply in one to three
            sentences, as a score.'; for :patch, the text and the :brief.
          (parse-reply raw) -> the JSON object in a model's reply as
            Clojure data with string keys, or {:error kw}: the reply may
            wrap it in a ```json fence or put prose around it; take the
            first balanced {...} that parses.
          (->score data) -> {:score x :unfound [phrase ...]}: the reply as
            the data lab.score/normalize takes. Keys and enum values
            become keywords (\"kind\" \"gesture\" \"curve\" \"channel\"
            \"wave\" \"phase\" \"order\" \"each\" \"as\" \"shot\", and
            \"style\" when it is a string); \"alternate\" and \"abs\" become
            :alternate? and :abs?; each mark's and dress's \"phrase\" is
            replaced by the :span of its first occurrence in the text (in
            UTF-16 units); a phrase that is not in the text is left out
            and listed in :unfound. Never throws.
          (measure case reply-text) -> one result map: :id :mode;
            :parsed? ; :valid? (normalize gave a score); :text-kept? (for
            :mark and :patch, the reply's text equals the case's text);
            :marks (count kept), :dropped (normalize's list), :unfound;
            :kinds (frequencies of mark kinds); :energy and :warmth (the
            mean over marks, missing as 0; nil with no marks);
            :gestures (named gestures used); :patches (count of marks that
            kept a :patch) and :patch-problems (count removed for
            problems, with lab.synth/problems' output); :dress (count);
            :style :shot.
          (summary results) -> the numbers for the notebook: n; the rates
            of :parsed?, :valid?, :text-kept? and 'clean' (valid with
            nothing dropped and nothing unfound); marks per reply (mean,
            min, max); the share of replies with no marks; kinds overall;
            for the :mark cases, per feeling, the mean energy and warmth,
            and the share whose warmth has the feeling's sign (tender +,
            furious -; wry is not scored) and whose energy has it (furious
            +, tender -); for the :patch cases, how many replies carried a
            patch and how many patches had no problems; total cost.
          I/O (thin, at the edge): (ask! {:system :user} opts) runs
            `claude -p <user> --system-prompt <system> --tools \"\"
            --disallowedTools \"mcp__*\" --output-format json` with a
            timeout (default 180 s), through an injectable :process-fn as
            halfahead.worker.engine does, and returns {:raw result-text
            :cost-usd n} or {:error ...}; a failure is a result with
            :parsed? false, never an exception.
          bb lab:score-eval [--only id-prefix] [--limit n] [--repeat k]:
            runs the cases one after another (never in parallel), prints a
            line per case and the summary as a table, and writes
            out/score-eval/report.edn ({:summary .. :results ..}, each
            result with the raw reply). It makes model calls and costs
            money: it prints the count before starting, and it is not part
            of `bb test`.
          Tests (no model calls): prompt for one case of each mode; parse
          of a bare object, a fenced one, one with prose around it, and
          junk; ->score for a reply with marks, dress, a patch (with
          \"alternate\" and \"abs\"), an unfound phrase and a string
          style; measure on canned replies: a clean one, one whose text
          was changed, one with a patch that does not end at rest (counted
          in :patch-problems, the mark kept), one that is not JSON;
          summary on a hand-made list of results with exact numbers; ask!
          with a fake :process-fn for success, non-zero exit and timeout."
 :acceptance
 ["score-eval tests as in the design; `bb test` stays green"
  "`bb lab:score-eval --limit 1` is NOT run by the factory: do not spend
   on model calls; say in the final message that the foreman runs it"]
 :non-goals
 ["No model calls in tests or in the order's own checks"
  "No change to the worker, the app, lab.score or the reference and cases"
  "Do not run `bb e2e`, `bb play` or `bb lab:e2e`"]
 :context ["docs/product/lab-notebook.md" "resources/agent/score-reference.md"
           "resources/eval/score-cases.edn" "src/halfahead/lab/score.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/marks.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/synth.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/worker/engine.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/engine_test.clj"
           "bb.edn" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
